1
00:00:05,410 --> 00:00:54,440
 blood vessels of the human body. Their surface area is 700,000 square meters. They measure more

2
00:00:54,440 --> 00:00:58,830
 than a hundred thousand kilometers in length. That's seven times the diameter of the globe.

3
00:00:59,950 --> 00:01:05,440
 Every day, the heart beats a hundred thousand times to keep blood circulating through these

4
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:19,600
 arteries and veins. Blood is the very stuff of life. One cubic millimeter of liquid blood plasma

5
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:22,370
 contains five million red corpuscles

6
00:01:22,370 --> 00:01:25,470
 and 700,000 phagocytes, or white.

7
00:01:27,020 --> 00:01:28,990
 They're the policemen of the bloodstream,

8
00:01:29,310 --> 00:01:31,230
 always on the lookout for germs.

9
00:01:33,530 --> 00:01:36,380
 Just a moment, quick, after them, officer.

10
00:01:37,730 --> 00:01:38,310
 To answer!

11
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:50,270
 Any problems, Lieutenant?

12
00:01:50,590 --> 00:01:53,950
 The lymphocyte patrol will always help the police in an emergency.

13
00:01:54,490 --> 00:01:56,270
 For the moment, all's well in this sector,

14
00:01:56,760 --> 00:02:01,220
 despite the heavy traffic flow of busy red corpuscles loaded with gas.

15
00:02:01,820 --> 00:02:03,690
 Grandpa, can't you walk any faster?

16
00:02:04,210 --> 00:02:10,780
 Young lady, I can see you've got no respect for your elders. Too bad.

17
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:15,340
 Sorry. Look here, Hemo, you don't seem to be your usual bright self today.

18
00:02:15,440 --> 00:02:19,740
 Well, you know how much I hate it when I've got an enormous load of carbon dioxide to deliver?

19
00:02:20,110 --> 00:02:23,130
 It brings me out in a sweat and I can't catch my breath.

20
00:02:24,010 --> 00:02:26,580
 It wouldn't bother me. What's this?

21
00:02:26,660 --> 00:02:29,800
 I'd rather carry oxygen any day. At least, you know, it's pure.

22
00:02:30,860 --> 00:02:34,270
 Come on, big fellow, cheer up, hmm? It's not far to the lungs now.

23
00:03:17,250 --> 00:03:39,790
 A policeman must sacrifice his own life to keep the bloodstream safe for others.

24
00:03:39,790 --> 00:03:41,360
 I didn't know he was dangerous.

25
00:03:41,640 --> 00:03:43,220
 You'll learn soon enough, my dear.

26
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:44,480
 Never trust a stranger.

27
00:03:45,370 --> 00:03:46,470
 Outsiders are dangerous.

28
00:03:47,020 --> 00:03:49,570
 Luckily, our police are always on the alert.

29
00:03:50,440 --> 00:03:51,280
 Come on, the show's over.

30
00:03:51,660 --> 00:03:52,280
 Move along there.

31
00:03:52,520 --> 00:03:52,940
 Get moving.

32
00:03:54,290 --> 00:03:55,930
 It's along there.

33
00:03:59,790 --> 00:04:00,990
 Hey, working in the lungs.

34
00:04:01,210 --> 00:04:02,510
 It won't be long now, Hemo.

35
00:04:02,590 --> 00:04:05,470
 We'll soon be out in the lovely fresh air and you'll get your oxygen.

36
00:04:29,610 --> 00:04:40,130
 No end.

37
00:05:16,530 --> 00:05:24,830
 Yes, and it's unbelievably boring to march around the same old route 4,000 times a day.

38
00:05:24,850 --> 00:05:28,030
 I'm quite happy to do it 365 days a year.

39
00:05:28,790 --> 00:05:32,300
 65 days, a very long lifespan for corpuscles like us.

40
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:36,220
 I hate to disillusion you, but our lives are much shorter, believe me.

41
00:05:36,650 --> 00:05:38,830
 A short life and a merry one, that's what I say.

42
00:05:41,850 --> 00:05:46,060
 Hey, you. Move along there.

43
00:05:46,460 --> 00:05:49,650
 I'm so sorry, officer. I didn't realize that you'd notice me.

44
00:05:50,770 --> 00:05:54,780
 Calling all sales, calling all sales.

45
00:05:55,160 --> 00:05:57,880
 Sugar in short supply, sugar in short supply.

46
00:05:58,170 --> 00:06:00,110
 Please release your reserves immediately.

47
00:06:00,230 --> 00:06:01,490
 Oh, was that my fault?

48
00:06:01,880 --> 00:06:03,230
 But of course not, my dear.

49
00:06:03,610 --> 00:06:05,780
 It's a general shortage in the whole sector.

50
00:06:05,780 --> 00:06:09,020
 Calling all cells make your reserve sugar available immediately.

51
00:06:09,400 --> 00:06:13,600
 Young people of today, no thought for the future, no organization, whatever.

52
00:06:14,060 --> 00:06:16,330
 Why, in my day, thought ahead.

53
00:06:17,090 --> 00:06:22,440
 Calling sugar stores, calling sugar stores, release some sugar immediately.

54
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:37,320
 Here control room, a signal goes out to the part of the cell where sugar is stored.

55
00:06:37,850 --> 00:06:38,860
 The Golgai bodies.

56
00:06:40,180 --> 00:06:44,820
 When the signal is received, sugar is released through the walls of the cell.

57
00:06:45,930 --> 00:06:47,800
 Soon the shortage will be over.

58
00:06:47,800 --> 00:07:05,650
 Better say goodbye to you now. I'm afraid that my journey through life is over.

59
00:07:05,930 --> 00:07:11,110
 But there's no reason to feel sad. We all live for 100 days, 120 at the outside.

60
00:07:11,400 --> 00:07:15,260
 And we do live a full life. Then we go to rest in the spleen.

61
00:07:17,030 --> 00:07:20,520
 I suppose you'll be coming along with me this time.

62
00:07:21,570 --> 00:07:25,440
 Me too. And me as well.

63
00:07:26,110 --> 00:07:31,990
 You're going to become of us after you've gone away. Two of us just can't cope with all that work on our own.

64
00:07:32,010 --> 00:07:35,650
 Do you know how quickly we are reborn? Over two million of us per second.

65
00:07:35,650 --> 00:07:38,750
 A million red corpuscles born per second?

66
00:07:38,750 --> 00:07:43,330
 Oh, but, Father dear, we really will miss you very much indeed.

67
00:07:43,330 --> 00:07:45,580
 Whatever will we do without your good advice?

68
00:07:45,580 --> 00:07:48,300
 Thank you, but I'll be back.

69
00:07:48,300 --> 00:07:49,570
 I promise.

70
00:07:49,570 --> 00:07:50,690
 Bye for now.

71
00:07:50,690 --> 00:07:51,700
 Bye.

72
00:08:21,440 --> 00:08:31,410
 In bloodstream, rate of breathing has been increased.

73
00:08:31,410 --> 00:08:33,470
 Report to your nearest cell on the double.

74
00:08:33,470 --> 00:08:41,020
 That's yours.

75
00:08:41,020 --> 00:08:44,730
 But never mind, Globin dear, it's not far now.

76
00:08:44,730 --> 00:08:52,770
 Go get him.

77
00:08:52,770 --> 00:09:13,580
 You want to report, Lieutenant?

78
00:09:13,580 --> 00:09:20,090
 ...is like you get on my nerves.

79
00:09:20,090 --> 00:09:21,060
 Idle.

80
00:09:21,060 --> 00:09:22,770
 That's what you are, idle.

81
00:09:22,770 --> 00:09:24,710
 What have we here?

82
00:09:25,210 --> 00:09:28,130
 Your job is to carry gases from one part of the body to another.

83
00:09:28,620 --> 00:09:29,790
 So get on with it then.

84
00:09:30,010 --> 00:09:30,650
 Yes, sir.

85
00:09:35,690 --> 00:09:45,470
 I've got more than a full load on my back already.

86
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:47,200
 We're not slaves, are we?

87
00:09:47,400 --> 00:09:48,860
 We'll just have to take on more workers.

88
00:09:52,040 --> 00:09:55,100
 They'll just have to work much faster, Lieutenant.

89
00:09:55,650 --> 00:09:57,690
 Uh, um, that's not going to work.

90
00:09:57,960 --> 00:09:59,440
 We'll use another method instead.

91
00:10:00,500 --> 00:10:02,440
 Send in the macrophage units.

92
00:10:06,140 --> 00:10:15,660
 That seems to have cleared up the blockage.

93
00:10:15,720 --> 00:10:17,360
 Now let's get those red corpuscles moving.

94
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:17,840
 Come on.

95
00:10:18,040 --> 00:10:18,940
 All right, let's go.

96
00:10:21,840 --> 00:10:22,930
 Uh-oh.

97
00:10:23,410 --> 00:10:24,650
 That's all we need.

98
00:10:26,630 --> 00:10:28,770
 Possible invasion. Please send patrol urgently.

99
00:10:35,520 --> 00:10:36,520
 Calling all units.

100
00:10:37,410 --> 00:10:39,790
 Investigate suspected alien invaders without delay.

101
00:10:40,030 --> 00:10:42,450
 Repeat. Investigate suspected alien invaders.

102
00:10:47,220 --> 00:10:50,820
 Just a second.

103
00:10:51,580 --> 00:10:53,080
 I hope you have no objections, sir.

104
00:10:53,300 --> 00:10:55,590
 But I must ask for your identity card.

105
00:10:55,960 --> 00:10:58,060
 It's just to prove that you don't come from outside the body.

106
00:11:06,720 --> 00:11:10,310
 Invasion, send reinforcements!

107
00:11:11,370 --> 00:12:02,980
 But it was nothing out of the ordinary, sir.

108
00:12:03,270 --> 00:12:05,560
 These streptococci are all in a day's work around here.

109
00:12:05,560 --> 00:12:07,600
 Send in sanitation squad immediately.

110
00:12:07,740 --> 00:12:09,500
 Operation successfully concluded.

111
00:12:12,920 --> 00:12:21,980
 Everybody, the show's over. Let's get moving.

112
00:12:22,470 --> 00:12:23,720
 On your way, Corpuscles.

113
00:12:24,630 --> 00:12:26,980
 Bye, Lieutenant. Take care, Captain.

114
00:12:48,870 --> 00:13:04,000
 It is sneezing.

115
00:13:05,040 --> 00:13:09,760
 Well, it seems that some of the white corpuscle policemen in his body are asleep on duty.

116
00:13:10,260 --> 00:13:11,940
 Exhausted by their recent battle.

117
00:13:13,180 --> 00:13:17,940
 This very moment, a small party of viruses appear.

118
00:13:18,020 --> 00:13:20,760
 We're nearly there, man. Come on.

119
00:13:22,690 --> 00:13:25,570
 We're creeping while they guard us down.

120
00:13:29,180 --> 00:13:35,680
 Surprise attack is finally noticed by a swarm of tiny antibodies.

121
00:13:37,080 --> 00:13:38,940
 Just swat them and keep going.

122
00:13:40,010 --> 00:13:52,770
 The nuclear control room of the cell, all is calm.

123
00:13:53,470 --> 00:13:54,330
 Too calm, perhaps.

124
00:14:04,790 --> 00:14:12,100
 Hang on here, for goodness sake, we're under attack.

125
00:14:13,660 --> 00:14:15,980
 Cell number 4714 reporting.

126
00:14:16,200 --> 00:14:17,950
 We're under heavy attack by type B flu viruses.

127
00:14:18,230 --> 00:14:19,430
 Please pass on the information.

128
00:14:20,350 --> 00:14:21,820
 Right away, right away.

129
00:14:22,060 --> 00:14:22,860
 But who's this now?

130
00:14:25,980 --> 00:14:29,150
 That's it.

131
00:14:29,250 --> 00:14:32,550
 I'm calling a general alert for all the cells in the 4,000 sector.

132
00:14:32,830 --> 00:14:34,610
 Calling all cells, general alert.

133
00:14:34,850 --> 00:14:37,070
 We're under attack by type B flu virus.

134
00:14:37,290 --> 00:14:39,610
 All antibody defenders to their stations immediately.

135
00:14:39,980 --> 00:14:40,790
 Hello, police.

136
00:14:40,930 --> 00:14:42,010
 Come in, police.

137
00:14:42,010 --> 00:14:42,990
 Come in, police.

138
00:14:43,170 --> 00:14:43,970
 This is an emergency.

139
00:14:44,380 --> 00:14:46,620
 Oh, why can't I get through when I need them urgently?

140
00:14:46,860 --> 00:14:48,000
 Calling police patrol.

141
00:14:58,850 --> 00:15:07,250
 To sanitation squad, hello?

142
00:15:07,740 --> 00:15:08,050
 Hello?

143
00:15:08,830 --> 00:15:11,690
 Attachment of macrophages to junction number seven, please.

144
00:15:17,050 --> 00:15:23,420
 Get an important job to do.

145
00:15:23,710 --> 00:15:24,660
 I don't agree, you know.

146
00:15:25,040 --> 00:15:26,880
 I think you do a very important task.

147
00:15:27,130 --> 00:15:30,580
 For example, a minute ago you helped to clear the circulation.

148
00:15:31,020 --> 00:15:32,570
 Yes, it wasn't essential.

149
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:35,210
 That may be so, but there are other tasks that come.

150
00:15:35,310 --> 00:15:37,650
 When we will be lost without you, platelets, you'll see.

151
00:15:38,870 --> 00:15:39,350
 Platelets.

152
00:15:39,610 --> 00:15:42,110
 Calling police patrol.

153
00:15:42,310 --> 00:15:43,670
 Come in, police patrol.

154
00:15:43,830 --> 00:15:45,950
 Why can't I contact you when I need you most?

155
00:15:46,070 --> 00:15:46,650
 Come in, patrol.

156
00:15:47,430 --> 00:15:49,670
 Lieutenant Claire of the patrol squad at your service.

157
00:15:49,910 --> 00:15:51,390
 At last, not before time.

158
00:15:51,470 --> 00:15:53,110
 You're never there when you're needed, are you?

159
00:15:53,570 --> 00:15:55,280
 This is cell number 4715.

160
00:15:55,580 --> 00:15:57,260
 We've got a viral invasion in our sector.

161
00:15:57,380 --> 00:15:57,520
 Hurry.

162
00:15:57,700 --> 00:15:58,800
 This is Captain Peter speaking.

163
00:15:58,960 --> 00:16:00,080
 We are now on our way.

164
00:16:34,140 --> 00:17:10,270
 Take over a cell and start multiplying inside it.

165
00:17:11,460 --> 00:17:11,820
 Precisely.

166
00:17:11,960 --> 00:17:13,880
 Now, are you going to hang about till it's my turn?

167
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:16,180
 Can't you see how serious the situation is?

168
00:17:16,380 --> 00:17:17,810
 We don't have a moment to lose.

169
00:17:18,220 --> 00:17:21,640
 Lieutenant Jumbo, take your ground forces to within striking distance of the enemy.

170
00:17:21,640 --> 00:17:23,060
 Wait for my signal to attack.

171
00:17:23,080 --> 00:17:29,100
 The lymphocyte ship squadron will provide air cover, take up position, and wait for my order to commence antibody bombardment.

172
00:17:32,550 --> 00:17:38,350
 Lieutenant Clare, we'll stay here in reserve with the lasers. Send a signal to General Headquarters.

173
00:17:39,150 --> 00:17:43,950
 All right now, men. Polynuclear infantry, up an atom, and show these aliens no mercy.

174
00:17:44,850 --> 00:18:47,230
 Yes, sir. They type B flu viruses.

175
00:18:47,310 --> 00:18:52,610
 Evidently, sir. We've dealt with them before, and we feel confident that we can handle them now. We've been vaccinated.

176
00:18:52,890 --> 00:18:54,670
 Well, carry on, Captain Peter, and good luck.

177
00:18:54,670 --> 00:19:00,690
 All right now, Lieutenant. I want you to defend the healthy cells. That's the only way we'll stop the virus multiplying.

178
00:19:00,890 --> 00:19:02,310
 Very good, Captain. I understand.

179
00:19:02,770 --> 00:19:10,680
 Calling commanders of antibody units, confirm your combat-ready status and prepare to drop into battle zone objective to defend cells against viral attack.

180
00:19:11,010 --> 00:19:12,330
 Metro, are your men ready?

181
00:19:12,880 --> 00:19:14,740
 Ready? You must be joking.

182
00:19:15,530 --> 00:19:21,470
 There's a question. You know very well that my splendid body of men has been spoiling for a fight ever since it was formed.

183
00:19:21,470 --> 00:19:24,150
 That's enough of that, Metro. There's no time for boasting now.

184
00:19:24,150 --> 00:19:27,680
 What I want from you is a straight answer to a straight question. Is that clear?

185
00:19:27,920 --> 00:19:31,760
 I'm sending you down there to protect cells. Are you equipped to deal with the enemy?

186
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:33,400
 Yes, we're trained and vaccinated.

187
00:19:33,710 --> 00:19:34,680
 Let's go then.

188
00:19:35,080 --> 00:19:36,420
 Follow me, men. Let's jump.

189
00:19:54,720 --> 00:20:03,020
 We're promised.

190
00:21:13,900 --> 00:21:15,180
 Situation report, Lieutenant.

191
00:21:15,180 --> 00:21:19,880
 Yes, sir. We are engaging the enemy and blocking their advance, but they're not beaten yet, I'm afraid.

192
00:21:20,380 --> 00:21:21,410
 Yes, Lieutenant Claire.

193
00:21:21,710 --> 00:21:27,590
 My antibody troops can't contain them, sir. They multiply far too rapidly. We need reinforcements as soon as possible.

194
00:21:27,910 --> 00:21:29,670
 I'm afraid we'll have to cope on our own, Lieutenant.

195
00:21:29,830 --> 00:21:33,370
 General headquarters entrusted us with this mission and we cannot let them down.

196
00:21:34,210 --> 00:21:35,990
 After all, it's only a regional conflict.

197
00:21:36,270 --> 00:21:38,010
 I'm sure that we have the resources to handle it.

198
00:21:38,310 --> 00:21:39,870
 Now, here's what our next move will be.

199
00:21:40,680 --> 00:21:42,440
 I'm going to order a cell division maneuver.

200
00:21:42,800 --> 00:21:45,060
 General cell division, then artillery support.

201
00:21:45,550 --> 00:21:47,450
 Calling all corpuscle ground forces.

202
00:21:47,730 --> 00:21:50,590
 You're ordered to execute a strategic withdrawal immediately.

203
00:22:03,740 --> 00:22:08,340
 Bind ground and air forces.

204
00:22:08,730 --> 00:22:10,880
 Calling all white corpuscles and lymphocytes.

205
00:22:11,180 --> 00:22:13,240
 Prepare to carry out Operation Mitosis.

206
00:22:13,560 --> 00:22:14,300
 Wait for my order.

207
00:22:14,780 --> 00:22:15,810
 Ready, divide!

208
00:22:15,930 --> 00:22:28,390
 Heat the maneuver as soon as you're ready.

209
00:22:28,390 --> 00:22:41,660
 Toxic lasers at will.

210
00:22:41,660 --> 00:22:44,730
 Take careful aim men, we don't want to harm our sight.

211
00:22:44,730 --> 00:23:16,990
 Sad, there's no point in getting all upset, especially over a white corpuscle.

212
00:23:16,990 --> 00:23:26,540
 I've had a pretty good innings for a corpuscle, I suppose. About time I was recycled.

213
00:23:26,540 --> 00:23:34,560
 That's it, all the excitement's over for now. Move along there. Move along!

